Falsifies `xtask::swish_check::boot::swish_check_boot`, the `installed/unvouched` line of its script.

Architecture: aarch64
Line: installed/unvouched

Milestone 673 (the confinement table lists the unvouched child), row 31 of
notes/confinement-claims.md. `script/falsifications --sweep xtask` replays it since milestone 742
(provisional): it boots `script/swish-check --arch aarch64` with this patch applied and calls it
red only when swish-check's FAILED report names the `Line:` above. By hand, the same thing is:

    git apply xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.swish_check_boot.patch
    script/swish-check --arch aarch64        # must exit non-zero, failing `installed/unvouched`
    git apply -R xtask/falsifications/swish_check.boot.swish_check_boot.patch

The defect is the progenitor endowing the process domain to a child whose bytes nobody vouched for
(`wants_domain` true whatever the manifest says). The domain is the first of the three authorities
the fixture `installed/unvouched` (`unreachable_network_witness`, stripped so no table vouches for
it) probes with a real request, and the table in notes/packages/running-unvouched.md records the
same defect for entropy and the network, each turned red by hand once (commit b555bfb3d). This
record is the one of the three that can be replayed.

The process domain came with milestone 126 (the `procps` package: who else is running, and who is
allowed to ask).

Expected to fail: the `installed/unvouched` line wants `domain: refused (no capability at slot 7)`
and `slots held: 0 1 2\n`, and the child reports `domain: REACHED` and `slots held: 0 1 2 7`.

Re-cut 2026-10-15 (UTC) by the lane proving milestone 898 (`swish_check_boot` is decomposed into
its phases): the sweep found this patch no longer compiled, because the vouch decision moved out
of `spawn_service` into `resolve`, and `Wants::of` had no `unvouched` in scope to believe. The
same defect, threaded through today's shape: `resolve` carries `unvouched` on `Resolved`,
`spawn_job` passes it, and an unvouched image's domain request is believed exactly as before. Red
again at `installed/unvouched` on aarch64, same sentence. The hunk's context cites §92 (a caretaker is supervised by the client it serves), the supervision
the region split serves.

diff --git a/crates/system_initializer/src/spawn_loop.rs b/crates/system_initializer/src/spawn_loop.rs
